{
  "_comment": "Core runs a chain once per file. The model writes the steps as for one file with the batch glob as the first step's input (the per-file rule, owner 2026-10-14); core repeats them for every file the glob matched. A later step is in the chain when it reads a chain step's output: by its name (the per-file form) or by its pattern (`rotated/*.mkv`); core accepts both links. A joining tool reading a chain output reads every file's, in input order (fan-in). Names (owner, 2026-10-15): the input's name with the extension the step writes, next to the input; a pattern's * is the input's name, in the pattern's folder when it has one. On a clash with a batch input or an earlier output of the lift, the model's label is added (`dog_trimmed.mp4`), then a counter. `expand` is what the caller found for each glob, in input order. Order: each file goes through the whole chain before the next (per file; won the run-order A/B against step by step, 2026-10-20). Python `knaif.batch_chain.lift_per_file_chain`, Rust `knaif_core::batch_chain`. Each case's `lift` records which file every lifted step works on (`file_of`, an index into `files`, null outside the chain), each file as reports show it (`shown`), and where every entry of a join came from (`join_files`, by the join's index in the lifted plan); `home` and `single` are lift_batch's options.",
  "joining_tools": [
    "concat_video",
    "merge_pdfs"
  ],
  "_batch_outputs": "Tools that write their result to a file only when core repeats them over many files (tools.yaml `batch_output:`, owner 2026-10-20): a lifted step of one with no output of its own gets the batch file's name with this extension, next to it. A single-file step is not lifted and keeps printing.",
  "batch_outputs": {
    "extract_text": "txt"
  },
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "a_name_link_runs_the_chain_once_per_file",
      "_note": "The model's label (clip) never reaches a file name: input name + the new extension.",
      "expand": {
        "*.mov": [
          "beach.mov",
          "city.mov"
        ]
      },
      "plan": [
        {
          "tool": "convert_video",
          "args": {
            "inputs": [
              "*.mov"
            ],
            "container": "mp4",
            "output": "clip.mp4"
          }
        },
        {
          "tool": "extract_audio",
          "args": {
            "inputs": [
              "clip.mp4"
            ],
            "audio_format": "mp3"
          }
        }
      ],
      "expected": [
        {
          "tool": "convert_video",
          "args": {
            "inputs": [
              "beach.mov"
            ],
            "container": "mp4",
            "output": "beach.mp4"
          }
        },
        {
          "tool": "extract_audio",
          "args": {
            "inputs": [
              "beach.mp4"
            ],
            "audio_format": "mp3"
          }
        },
        {
          "tool": "convert_video",
          "args": {
            "inputs": [
              "city.mov"
            ],
            "container": "mp4",
            "output": "city.mp4"
          }
        },
        {
          "tool": "extract_audio",
          "args": {
            "inputs": [
              "city.mp4"
            ],
            "audio_format": "mp3"
          }
        }
      ],
      "lift": {
        "files": [
          "beach.mov",
          "city.mov"
        ],
        "shown": [
          "beach.mov",
          "city.mov"
        ],
        "file_of": [
          0,
          0,
          1,
          1
        ],
        "join_files": {}
      }
    },
